# Dev Tools
#
# List of dev tools I prefer. The list is ordered: of two tools that share a
# tag, the one written first is preferred. The configuration in this repo
# mostly revolves around these tools, and a few more. This file is under
# development, so more tools will be added.
#
# Only current tools and AI tools go here. Tools I tried, used before, or want
# to try go in work dev_tools_archive.md:
# https://github.com/raveensrk/work/blob/main/deck/tools/dev_tools_archive.md
# A tool lives in one file only.
#
# Tags say what a tool is; any word or phrase, one Tag line each. They began
# as the old fields, so these mean what they meant:
#   base, extra, max       how much a tool matters: the core kit, what I use
#                          often, everything (the first tag; it sets the colour)
#   beginner               useful within minutes
#   easy                   the basics take a few hours
#   intermediate           takes days; has its own concepts or config to learn
#   advanced               takes weeks; needs a deep mental model
#   expert                 takes months or years to master
#   Terminal, AI, ...      what kind of tool it is
#
# The learning path is the Edge records: From must be known before To. Every
# edge into a tool is required (AND); edges that share an Any value are
# either-one (OR). There are no loops, and a prerequisite already implied
# through another one is not repeated. The %graph lines say so, and
# draw_graph enforces them.
#
# Edit:   draw_graph dev_tools.rec   (a graph editor: https://github.com/raveensrk/draw_graph)
# Check:  draw_graph check dev_tools.rec
# Query:  recsel -t Node -e 'Tag = "base"' -p Name dev_tools.rec
#         recsel -t Edge -e 'To = "Rust"' -p From dev_tools.rec
# Pos is where draw_graph shows a tool, `x y` in px; layout only. Group puts
# a tool in a named box (Group: Browser).

%rec: Group
%key: Name
%type: Parent rec Group
%type: Collapsed enum yes no
%allowed: Name Label Parent Color Collapsed Note
%graph: parent Parent

Name: LLM data

Name: Browser

Name: VPN

%rec: Node
%key: Name
%type: Group rec Group
%type: Pos regexp /^-?[0-9]+ -?[0-9]+$/
%mandatory: Name
%allowed: Name Tag Url Note Group Pos
%graph: label Name
%graph: tag Tag
%graph: color Tag
%graph: group Group
%graph: pos Pos

